{
  "name": "Occult Association: Goetic Summoner (Tier 2)",
  "type": "feat",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><strong>Tier 2 — Goetic Summoner</strong></p><p><strong>“You don’t fight the corruption. You aim it.”</strong></p><p>At Tier 2, you stop pretending the veil is a barrier. It is a marketplace.</p><p>You have enough practice to exploit corrupted environments without being swallowed by them. Usually. Your faction becomes frighteningly competent in places others cannot operate.</p><p><strong>Strategic (Faction Scale)</strong></p><ul><li>When dealing with Qliphothic entities or running Scenarios in corrupted Hexes, gain <strong>Advantage</strong> on one relevant Strategic Roll per Scenario</li><li>If the opposition is attempting to deceive, terrorize, or destabilize via Darkness-as-pressure, gain <strong>+1 to the relevant Intrigue OP roll</strong> instead</li></ul><p><strong>Cost:</strong> every time you leverage this understanding, the GM is encouraged to record a <strong>Debt</strong> in the fiction. Not a number. A <em>name</em>.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
